Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:42:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] refactor(research): derive focus tags from overlays and
 distinctive pathways

Tier-default pathways (quality, observability, release, docs) were pulling
noise tags like ai-agents and seo into every research card. Derivation now:

- every tag whose overlays intersect the item's overlays is derived;
- a pathway counts only when distinctive: in the itinerary, not a default of
  PATHWAY_TIERS[tier], not required by a present overlay, and not research.

research_focus_for gains a tier argument (pathway-next passes contract_tier);
RESEARCH_FOCUS_OVERLAY_WEIGHT is removed. A live npm-CVE item with
supply-chain now renders "/research-stack --deep --focus security,devtools".
Tests and the reference doc updated; documented count is now 1181.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LWfLzbXaVEAGYrKt39r4bc
